{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"fdf6ee1a91bff1edb92a7dfee727f8aed87a10deea1966f87187b0e060ce78fc","digest":{"component_or_area":"CLI bridge command structure and verb naming","key_entities":["rebar bridge fsck","rebar bridge check-access","rebar bridge setup","bridge-fsck","bridge-probe","jira-onboard","src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py","src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py","src/rebar/schemas/bridge_fsck.schema.json","src/rebar/_cli/_jira_onboard.py","src/rebar/_engine/jira-capability-probe.py","scripts/canary_bridge.py",".github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml","docs/cli-reference.md"],"problem_keywords":["CLI verb rename","command line interface","bridge noun-based naming","compatibility entrypoint","consumer migration"],"propositions":["Three CLI verbs are renamed to noun-based spellings: bridge-fsck becomes bridge fsck, bridge-probe becomes bridge check-access, and jira-onboard becomes bridge setup.","Old verb spellings remain as compatibility entrypoints that route to the same parser and implementation paths without forking behavior, state, exit policy, or output schema.","Every enumerated consumer of the three verbs must be migrated including CLI entry points, help text, schema IDs and descriptions, test assertions on literal string names, scripts, workflows, and documentation.","The bridge setup subcommand delegates to the existing jira_onboard parser via pass-through with entrypoint-specific prog value while preserving all options and validation flow.","bridge check-access ships as its own primary verb (not a flag on fsck) and performs the same create/label/search/delete Jira round-trip as legacy bridge-probe.","Behavioral parity is proven for both old and new spellings across success, failure, options, output, and exit status dimensions, with no removal of old spellings permitted without future separate deprecation tracking."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787353229632553001,"uuid":"6a3facbc-40ca-4de5-b0f2-b79b21b83d04"}